> >  > setCdf(ds, cdf);

First, you do not have to set the CDF explicitly *if* (and only if)
the CDF chip type is identical to the one you use to setup the CEL
set, i.e. the last two rows changes nothing - that CDF is already set
by default.

Second, if you do want to override the default CDF, you can now also
do it as follows:

cdf <- AffymetrixCdfFile$fromChipType("HuEx-1_0-st-v2,coreR2,A20070914,EP");
cs <- AffymetrixCelSet$fromName("anth", cdf=cdf);

This will setup you CEL set names 'anth' and downstream
queries/analysis will use the CDF 'HuEx-1_0-st-v2,coreR2,A20070914,EP'
that Elizabeth and other kindly provides.

